{"author":{"id":"2de4467f26c42fb223f4d3ddd5611e7c0513d3daae4c1dc315de039036bc997d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778952310,"nonce":"GKjQoIjmvTk/oh8VbSe5IasRpTk=","title":"Reduce search and social icon payload","message":"## Problem\nThe site has avoidable client/network weight in non-core UI.\n\nCurrent evidence:\n- Opening search lazy-loads full `highlight.js`, producing a dynamic chunk around 956 KB raw / 298 KB gzip in the local static export.\n- The homepage preloads several remote Simple Icons images from `cdn.simpleicons.org` for social links.\n- Search fetches a single `public/search/index.json` that is already around 592 KB for the current content set.\n\n## Context\nThe first-load shared JS is not terrible for a Next site, and search highlighting is lazy. The opportunity is to make occasional features cheaper and more robust, especially because this is a mostly static personal site.\n\n## Potential Solutions\n- For search snippets, avoid client-side `highlight.js`, or import only known languages, or precompute highlighted code snippets at build time.\n- Inline or vendor social SVGs locally instead of remote icon image requests.\n- Consider splitting/search-index compression or indexing fewer snippet fields if the index grows with private posts and series content.\n- Audit font preloads after simplifying typography choices.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}